From: TB520FU port maintainers
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: qcom: q6apm: handle SPF state timeout and defer until ADSP ready

The ADSP takes several seconds to bring up SPF after PDR audio_pd is
reported UP. q6apm_get_apm_state() sends APM_CMD_GET_SPF_STATE
(0x01001021) immediately in apm_probe() and ignores the return value
from q6apm_send_cmd_sync(), returning the stale apm->state (0) after a
5 s CMD timeout. The probe then returns 0 with the wrong state, and
once the sync error is propagated q6apm_is_adsp_ready() would convert
that negative error to boolean true.

Observed on TB520FU log2 boot: GPR service 2:1 added at 3.815 s,
apm_driver_init at 3.830 s, "CMD timeout for [1001021]" at 8.927 s,
"probe of gprsvc:service:2:1 returned 0 after 5101235 usecs". The second
query from q6prm succeeds quickly once SPF is up, proving the first
packet was sent before the DSP service was ready. The repeated
"Handover signaled, but it already happened" is benign: qcom_pas_attach()
pre-sets handover_issued when the bootloader left ADSP running, so the
spurious post-attach IRQ is expected and not the timeout cause.

Check the sync return, propagate the error, make is_adsp_ready() return
false on error, and defer apm_probe() with -EPROBE_DEFER (clearing g_apm)
so the core retries after the DSP is ready instead of registering with
stale state.

--- a/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6apm.c
+++ b/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6apm.c
@@ -151,20 +151,29 @@
 {
 	struct gpr_pkt *pkt __free(kfree) = audioreach_alloc_apm_cmd_pkt(0,
 								APM_CMD_GET_SPF_STATE, 0);
+	int ret;
 	if (IS_ERR(pkt))
 		return PTR_ERR(pkt);
 
-	q6apm_send_cmd_sync(apm, pkt, APM_CMD_RSP_GET_SPF_STATE);
+	ret = q6apm_send_cmd_sync(apm, pkt, APM_CMD_RSP_GET_SPF_STATE);
+	if (ret)
+		return ret;
 
 	return apm->state;
 }
 
 bool q6apm_is_adsp_ready(void)
 {
-	if (g_apm)
-		return q6apm_get_apm_state(g_apm);
+	int ret;
+
+	if (!g_apm)
+		return false;
 
-	return false;
+	ret = q6apm_get_apm_state(g_apm);
+	if (ret < 0)
+		return false;
+
+	return ret;
 }
 EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(q6apm_is_adsp_ready);
 
@@ -890,7 +899,12 @@
 
 	g_apm = apm;
 
-	q6apm_get_apm_state(apm);
+	ret = q6apm_get_apm_state(apm);
+	if (ret < 0) {
+		g_apm = NULL;
+		return dev_err_probe(dev, -EPROBE_DEFER,
+				     "ADSP SPF not ready (%d), deferring\n", ret);
+	}
 
 	ret = snd_soc_register_component(dev, &q6apm_audio_component, NULL, 0);
 	if (ret < 0) {
